4. Complexity Analysis
Let n be the length of the string.
Part	Complexity
Precompute substring costs	\(O(n^3 \log n)\) upper bound
Dynamic Programming	\(O(kn^2)\)
Space	\(O(n^2+nk)\)

- Time Complexity: \(O(n^3\log n+kn^2)\)
- Space Complexity: \(O(n^2+nk)\)
Important points:
1. A substring of length 1 cannot be a semi-palindrome, so every partition must contain substrings of length at least 2.
2. We try only proper divisors of the substring length.
3. The DP guarantees exactly k non-overlapping substrings.
4. We precompute costs so that DP transitions are \(O(1)\).
This solution handles the constraint \(n\leq 200\).

